{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Far be it.</b> A thing that cannot be. And some say the word is like the sense of חלול, that has nothing in it." "<b>And that the righteous be as the wicked.</b> When two kaf's are joined, it is an elliptical form, and the sense is: and let the righteous be as the wicked, and the wicked as the righteous. Likewise \"for you are as Pharaoh\" (Genesis 44:18), \"as my people, as your people\" (1 Kings 22:4), \"as darkness, as light\" (Psalms 139:12). And how is it possible that He who is judge of all the earth would not do justice?"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:00.287463448Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}